Job Summary

Langan is seeking a Field Technician - Geotechnical
to join its collaborative team in Salt Lake City, UT
. This individual will serve a key function in providing field inspections and testing services related to geotechnical investigations, earthwork, shallow foundations, ground improvement, and deep foundation construction. In this role, you will have the opportunity to work in a fast-paced outdoor environment, collaborate with experienced engineering professionals, and support a diverse range of projects with opportunities for travel.

Job Responsibilities

Perform field inspections related to logging borings and test pits, earthwork, shallow foundations, ground improvement, and deep foundations including augercast piles, driven piles, and drilled shafts;
Prepare daily field inspection reports and ensure all documentation and data sheets are accurate and up-to-date;
Oversee and document residential grout monitoring activities for sinkhole remediation projects;
Install and maintain seismograph vibration monitors, download and manage monitoring data, and assist with pre-construction condition documentation;
Support the preparation of monitoring reports and project documentation;
Maintain and troubleshoot field equipment as necessary;
Coordinate field activities with contractors and project teams to ensure quality and compliance with project requirements; and
Perform other duties as requested.

Qualifications

Associate’s degree in Engineering Technology, Construction Management, or a related field preferred; equivalent experience will be considered;
2+ years of related geotechnical field technician experience;
Construction or technology-related experience preferred, including logging borings, foundation subgrade and bearing zone inspections, earthwork testing, and Nuclear Gauge certification;
Proficiency with Microsoft Office Suite;
Excellent written and verbal communication skills;
Strong attention to detail with excellent analytical, multitasking, and judgment capabilities;
Ability to effectively work independently and in a team environment;
Possess reliable transportation to access job sites and a valid driver's license in good standing; and
Ability to spend up to 100% of work hours in the field.

Langan provides a rich array of programs and benefits to help its employees advance their careers and enhance the quality of their lives. Our comprehensive compensation package includes: full-time employment company paid medical, dental, and vision coverage; life insurance, short- and long-term disability insurance, and paid pregnancy disability leave; 401(k)/Roth with company match; paid time off including parental and military leave; employee referral and professional license bonuses; and educational reimbursement.

Langan offers employee resource groups; flexible work schedules; extensive training; wellness programs; buddy and mentoring programs; and much more!

Langan is committed to providing equal employment opportunities to all qualified applicants and employees, including individuals with disabilities and protected veterans. We believe that an inclusive workplace is essential for the well-being and success of our employees.

